##gtf-version 2.2
##description THE METHOD-DEVELOPMENT TEST TRANSCRIPTOME — hand-edited, one transcript at a time.
##
## ⭐⭐⭐ THIS FILE IS THE BENCHMARK, AND IT IS EMPTY ON PURPOSE (owner, 2026-08-27). The message
## policy is developed against a chromosome the owner designs transcript by transcript: add one
## structure, check the policy solves it AND everything already here, then add the next.
##
## ⛔ IT WAS CLEARED ON 2026-08-27 and starts again at ZERO transcripts. The previous 42 are in git
## history (`git log -- scripts/sim/test_reference/test_chr.gtf`) if a structure is ever wanted back.
##
## ── HOW TO ADD A TRANSCRIPT ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
##
## 1. Add one `exon` line per exon, here. GTF is 1-based and end-inclusive:
##
##      test_chr  rigel_test  exon  START  END  .  STRAND  .  gene_id "G1"; transcript_id "T1";
##
##    Exons of one transcript must not overlap, every intron must be at least 4 bp (it needs room
##    for a GT..AG motif), and every coordinate must fall inside the 1,000,000 bp chromosome.
##
## 2. Add its sampling weights to `test_abundances.tsv` — one row per transcript_id. The builder
##    REFUSES a transcript with no abundance row and an abundance row with no transcript.
##
## 3. Optionally add capture probes to `test_probes.bed` (BED12, 0-based half-open).
##
## 4. Rebuild everything derived, then simulate and cache — `docs/TESTING.md` §0a has the commands.
##
## ⭐ NASCENT RNA NEEDS NO DECLARATION: `rigel index` creates a single-exon nascent entity spanning
## each MULTI-EXON transcript. Give it weight through that transcript's `nrna_abundance` column.
##
## ⚠ κ (the strand-specificity model) IS FITTED FROM SPLICED READS, so a transcriptome of only
## single-exon transcripts cannot calibrate — `calibrate` raises `CalibrationStrandError`. At least
## one multi-exon transcript with real depth is required before a benchmark run means anything.
##
## ⭐ THE FASTA IS DERIVED FROM THIS FILE, never hand-edited: `build_test_reference.py` generates the
## 1,000,000 bp chromosome from a fixed seed and injects a GT..AG motif at every intron declared
## here, so the sequence can never disagree with the annotation.
##
## ⭐ NAME TRANSCRIPTS FOR WHAT THEY ARE. The convention that worked: strand, structure and SPLICED
## length — e.g. `T1p_SE_1KB` is a + strand single-exon transcript of 1,000 bp of exon.
##
## ── TRANSCRIPTS (none yet — add below this line) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
